  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Despite their very small size these fish are not at all very sensitive. The maximum length reported for Aphyoplatys duboisi is only 2.5 cm; the imported fish were about 1.5-2 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish have been collected in the surroundings of Brazzaville.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>It is the best choice to keep these jewels in small tanks on their own. Here the keeper has the best control over them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>If one wants to breed the fish, soft and slightly acidic water is recommended. The water level should be rather low, about 15 cm is best.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>These dwarf killis feed readily on dried food as well as on Artemia nauplii and comparatively small food items.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The males can be even a bit quarrelsome against each other, but they will not do real harm during combating.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/aphyoplatys_duboisi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish spawn readily, but raising the youngsters is sometimes a bit tricky. A. duboisi is a substrate spawner and the eggs do not need a dry period to hatch.</p>"
    }
  ],
